      "writtenOn": "2025-02-04T13:53:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was discussed in [this thread](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Connectivity/+/3315333/comment/bb0e33fb_d26e7c26/) as well.\n\nTo summarize:\nThis listener is registered during device boot with the ConnectivityService, and we plan topopulate the initial permission state after this registration (i.e. via the `startMonitoring` call). So, any permission changes (most commonly via user action) should occur after this registration has happened.\n\nRe: the AI suggested fix, `CompatChanges.isChangeEnabled(..)` is the only API available for checking the app compat change id and I don\u0027t see the import suggestions anywhere in other code. I\u0027m guessing the suggestion is inferred from feature flag notation?",
      "parentUuid": "14deff62_6b7a4549",
